From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz Madej <lukasz.madej.prv@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 25 May 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] bcmdhd: stop watchdog on suspend to release SDIO wakelock

On SDIO platforms (e.g. grinn-astra-1680-sbc) the BCM DHD driver holds
the wl_wdwake wakelock continuously while its periodic watchdog timer is
armed: dhd_os_wd_timer(wdtick > 0) takes the lock and only
dhd_os_wd_timer(0) releases it. On PCIe builds the same lock is taken
and released around each handler invocation, so it is effectively never
active when system suspend is attempted.

When the system enters suspend, bcmsdh_sdmmc_suspend() (func 2) calls
bcmsdh_suspend() -> dhdsdio_suspend(), which calls
dhd_os_check_wakelock(). The check returns 1 if wl_wifi or wl_wdwake is
active. The non-zero return is converted to -EBUSY by bcmsdh_suspend(),
aborting suspend with:

  bcmsdh_sdmmc mmc1:0001:2: PM: dpm_run_callback(): pm_generic_suspend returns -16
  bcmsdh_sdmmc mmc1:0001:2: PM: failed to suspend async: error -16

On the SBC the watchdog wakelock is held in 200-800 ms bursts (~20% of
the time), so suspend reliably fails. Hard-removing the WiFi module so
that the driver does not probe lets the system suspend correctly,
confirming the diagnosis.

Stop the watchdog timer in PM_SUSPEND_PREPARE (releasing wl_wdwake) and
re-arm it in PM_POST_SUSPEND. This is also semantically correct: the
WiFi watchdog has nothing to do while the chip is suspended.

Signed-off-by: Lukasz Madej <lukasz.madej.prv@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/synaptics/net/wireless/bcmdhd/dhd_linux.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/synaptics/net/wireless/bcmdhd/dhd_linux.c b/drivers/synaptics/net/wireless/bcmdhd/dhd_linux.c
--- a/drivers/synaptics/net/wireless/bcmdhd/dhd_linux.c
+++ b/drivers/synaptics/net/wireless/bcmdhd/dhd_linux.c
@@ -1113,5 +1113,11 @@ static int dhd_pm_callback(struct notifier_block *nfb, unsigned long action, voi
 	dhd_set_wowl_active(TRUE);
 	msleep(1000);
 #endif /* DHD_WOWL_IN_SUSPEND_SDIO */
+#ifdef BCMSDIO
+		/* Release wl_wdwake before SDIO suspend so that
+		 * dhd_os_check_wakelock() does not abort with -EBUSY. */
+		dhdinfo = container_of(nfb, dhd_info_t, pm_notifier);
+		dhd_os_wd_timer(&dhdinfo->pub, 0);
+#endif /* BCMSDIO */
 		suspend = TRUE;
 		break;
@@ -1121,6 +1127,10 @@ static int dhd_pm_callback(struct notifier_block *nfb, unsigned long action, voi
 #ifdef DHD_WOWL_IN_SUSPEND_SDIO
 	dhd_set_wowl_active(FALSE);
 #endif /* DHD_WOWL_IN_SUSPEND_SDIO */
+#ifdef BCMSDIO
+		dhdinfo = container_of(nfb, dhd_info_t, pm_notifier);
+		dhd_os_wd_timer(&dhdinfo->pub, dhd_watchdog_ms);
+#endif /* BCMSDIO */
 		suspend = FALSE;
 		break;
 	}
